# All configuration for `sync`, secret and not. Copy to `.env` (gitignored).
#
# In CI the same names come from repo *variables* (non-secret) and *secrets*
# (the two tokens) — see .github/workflows/sync.yml. Nothing is committed, which
# is what keeps every team's copy of this repo identical and `update` painless.

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Notion connection token, used to read the Skills Public API. REQUIRED.
# Needs read access to the skills you want published; that access IS the publish
# control — there is no per-skill publish flag.
# NOTION_API_TOKEN=ntn_xxx

# GitHub push token, needs push access to the target repo. If unset, the tool
# falls back to `gh auth token` for local runs.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx

# --- Where plugins are published --------------------------------------------

# The repo the sync writes to, as owner/name. REQUIRED.
# GITHUB_REPO=your-org/notion-skills
# Branch to write (default: main).
# GITHUB_BRANCH=main
# Commit identity (optional; defaults to a bot identity).
# GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=notion-skills-sync
# GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=notion-skills-sync@users.noreply.github.com

# --- Which Notion ------------------------------------------------------------

# prod (default) | dev | stg. Flips the API host and the page links written
# into plugin markers together.
# NOTION_ENV=prod

# The skills database's data source id. Recorded in each plugin's
# .notion-sync.json as the back-reference into Notion, and read to pull the
# grouping property's (the "Plugins" column's) per-option descriptions, which
# override each plugin's description when set. Not needed to *read* plugins; when
# unset or unreadable, the sync falls back to the API's plugin descriptions.
# For the override to work, share this data source with the sync's connection.
# SKILLS_DATA_SOURCE_ID=
